1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 4. O-O d6 5. c3 {Inferior to 5.d4, but then
Black gets a well-known variation of the Steinitz Defence.} Bd7 6. Re1 Be7 7.
d4 O-O 8. Nbd2 {Again, not good in this position. 8.h3 could be played to keep
the centre, or} (8. d5 Nb8 9. Bd3 {followed by c4 and Nc3}) 8... Nxd4 9. cxd4 {
The only move to save a pawn.} ({If} 9. Bxd7 Nxf3+) ({Or if} 9. Nxd4 exd4 10.
Bxd7 dxc3) 9... Bxb5 10. dxe5 dxe5 11. Qb3 ({If} 11. Nxe5 Qd4 12. Nef3 Qd3 13.
Qb3 ({or} 13. Ne5 {offering a draw.}) 13... Rad8 {gives Black the initiative.})
11... Ba6 12. Nxe5 Nd7 ({If} 12... Bc5 13. Ndf3 {and White completes his
development.}) 13. Nxd7 Qxd7 14. Nf3 Qb5 15. Qxb5 Bxb5 16. Bf4 c5 {Black has 3
v 2 pawns on the queenside as well as the bishop pair.} 17. Rac1 Rac8 18. Ne5
f6 ({If} 18... Bd6 19. Nd3) ({Or if} 18... Bf6 19. b3) ({If} 18... c4 19. Bd2 {
followed by Bc3.}) 19. Nc4 {Although this exchanges a bishop, it allows
Black's pawns to advance. Nf3 threatening e5 or Bd2, or Bd2 followed by Bc3
was rather better.} Bxc4 20. Rxc4 b5 21. Rc2 c4 22. Rd1 Rfd8 23. Rxd8+ Rxd8 24.
Kf1 Bb4 ({If} 24... Rd1+ 25. Ke2 Rg1 26. Kf3) 25. Ke2 Kf7 26. a3 Ba5 27. Bd2
Bb6 (27... Bxd2 {would give an ending in White's favour, as his King is nearer
Black's advanced pawns, but he had to play a6 first or else if 26.Bd2 a5.}) 28.
Bc3 Rd3 ({White expected the better move} 28... Ke6 {first, for if then} 29.
Rd2 ({Black did not want} 29. f4 Rd3 30. e5 Re3+ 31. Kf1 {but it does not seem
good enough for White.}) 29... Rxd2+ 30. Bxd2 ({not} 30. Kxd2 Bxf2) 30... Ke5
31. f3 Bd4 32. Bc3 a5 {with advantage.}) 29. Rd2 Rxd2+ 30. Bxd2 Bd4 31. Bc3 Be5
$2 {Sources: The Scotsman, 15 Aug 1938; Mallison's notebook. Contributor: Andy
Ansel.} (31... Bc5 {should be played giving a draw. N.B. This is the move
given in the printed sources - Manchester Guardian, 13 Aug 1938; Yorkshire
Post, 13 Aug 1938; Glasgow Herald, 16 Aug 1938}) (31... Be5 {White here too
hastily offered a draw, which was accepted, but then saw there was a win by}
32. Bxe5 fxe5 33. Kd2 Ke6 34. Kc3 (34. a4 b4) 34... Kd6 35. Kb4 Kc6 36. a4 a6 (
36... bxa4 37. h4) 37. axb5+ axb5 38. h4 $1 g6 39. g3 h6 40. f4 exf4 41. gxf4
Kb6 42. e5 {and wins.}) 1/2-1/2

