{"To Mrs Thomson who came second there occurred perhaps the most irritating
incident possible in chess. The following was the position at adjournment of
her game against Miss Dew, the former holder of the championship. Mrs Thomson
sealed the correct move:} 1... Qc5+ {. But a number of spectators manifested
displeasure at Mrs Thomson continuing what seemed to them an obviously drawn
game, and in deference to these 'authorities' Mrs Thomson agreed to a draw.
However, there is a win for Black in this position, e.g.} 2. Ka6 Qa3+ 3. Kb7
Qb4+ 4. Ka6 Qa4+ 5. Kb7 Qb5+ 6. Ka7 Kc7 {and White will soon be mated." 
(Source: BCM, Sept 1938, p417-418)} 1/2-1/2

