1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 Nf6 4. Nc3 Bg4 5. dxe5 Bxf3 6. Qxf3 dxe5 7. Bd2 Bc5 8.
O-O-O Qe7 9. Bg5 Nbd7 10. Nd5 Qd8 11. Bc4 c6 12. Nxf6+ gxf6 13. Rd3 Qe7 14.
Rhd1 O-O-O 15. Bh4 Rhg8 16. Qf5 Rg6 17. f4 Bb6 18. fxe5 Qxe5 19. Rxd7 Qxf5 20.
Rxd8+ Bxd8 21. exf5 Rxg2 22. Bxf7 Rxh2 23. Be6+ Kc7 24. Bg3+ {Source: Borough
of West Ham, East Ham and Stratford Express, 26 Aug 1938. The chess columnist,
F W Markwick, states that the game was played in a First Class tournament at
Hastings, but this appears to be wrong. In the same article he mentions that a
game between H H Cole and J Storr-Best (c.f. elsewhere in the database) was
also played at Hastings, though it is known that the game took place at the
BCF Congress at Brighton. Both E J Randall and A T Watson were in the 1st
Class 'C' event in the congress at Brighton. (Contributed by Brian Denman, who
also wrote the above note.)} 1-0

